ZTEXT00100000a79d21afab10000000
Zero filesystem driver ABI, revision 1

Drivers are original Zero state machines inside the monolithic kernel.
The same source runs in hosted test harnesses using Zero positioned I/O.
No external filesystem implementation is linked into the guest.

H = memory + 24576. Common request fields are unsigned 64-bit values:
  0 operation: 0 probe, 1 watch, 2 read, 3 create, 4 save, 5 remove
  8 ASCII name pointer
 16 name length, at most 31
 24 input pointer
 32 input length, at most 400
 40 output pointer
 48 output capacity including trailing NUL
 56 output length excluding NUL
 64 result
 72 caller completion state
 80 volume start in absolute 512-byte sectors
 88 volume length in 512-byte sectors
 96 format: 1 ext4, 2 NTFS, 3 Btrfs
104 flags: bit0 mounted, bit1 writable
136 listing policy:0 terminal entries,1 supported regular files only
    This extension occupies memory+24712, between root volume-management
    fields. Default0 preserves the existing terminal/driver ABI. The guest
    application service sets1 for its request and clears it before return.

Result: 0 success, 1 unsupported profile, 2 corrupt metadata, 3 I/O failure,
4 missing, 5 exists, 6 capacity exhausted, 7 invalid name/argument,
8 too large, 9 dirty/recovery required, 10 wrong format, 255 pending.
Wrong magic returns10; recognized unsupported features return1.
Names are flat ASCII, letters/digits/dot/underscore/hyphen; dot and dot-dot
are not valid file names. Save creates or replaces, create preserves existing.
Read and watch terminate output with NUL without exceeding output capacity.

Entry states: ext4 200, NTFS 300, Btrfs 400. All operations reload and validate
the selected volume, so switching drives does not reuse another drive's cache.
Completion writes result/output length then state=load64[H+72].
Root owns H..H+1023. Driver private memory is25600..32767.
Two16KiB buffers begin at memory+32768 and memory+49152.
Caller output uses memory+14336, capacity2044.
Do not overwrite root header, terminal, glyphs, scheduler, or ZeroFS cache.

Block I/O state90 takes io_lba absolute sector, io_buffer, io_count1..32,
io_write0 read/1 write/2 flush, io_return completion state. It returns io_ok.
disk_select identifies the physical ATA position0..3 and is root-owned.
Volatile scalar variables may be clobbered by I/O and terminal rendering;
store continuation state in driver-private memory. Preserve request header.
All requests must stay inside H+80/H+88 before invoking block I/O.
Mutations must preflight unsupported features and bounds before first write,
flush their documented transaction, and report failure rather than success
when durability or integrity is uncertain.
